.\" aliens-invaders.6x -- game manual (man 6). Simple English, portable macros.
.TH ALIENS-INVADERS 6 "2026" "Aliens Invaders" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
aliens-invaders \- modern C++20 / SDL3 arcade invasion game with a 15-movement
classical soundtrack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aliens-invaders
.RI [ option "] [" "track list" "] ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aliens-invaders
is a fast, deterministic arcade invasion game written in modern C++20 on top of
SDL3 (Vulkan by default, with automatic OpenGL fallback). Fifteen alien
armadas guard each stage cycle. Every stage is announced by a short classical
fanfare, synthesized live as a ten-instrument classical ensemble (violin,
viola, cello, double bass, flute, oboe, trumpet, French horn, piano, harp)
in 2.1 stereo: no audio files ship with the game.
.PP
Two synthesis engines share the same written scores. When a GM-compatible
SoundFont bank (\fB.sf2\fR) is installed, the soundtrack renders through
TinySoundFont with real instrument samples (CD-quality, the default);
otherwise \- and whenever \fB\-render\fR is passed \- the zero-asset
procedural synth takes over. A missing bank prints a one-time notice on
stderr naming the recommended bank (FluidR3 GM, MIT-licensed) and how to
install it.
.PP
Armada flight is continuous 60 Hz kinematics with subpixel render
interpolation: the formation drifts as a whole between cruise bounds, attack
dives follow inertial Catmull-Rom splines, every return to a honeycomb
station is a banked, rate-limited arc (never a sideways or backwards slide),
and hull attitudes turn in partitioned angular slices. No starship ever
teleports; motion stays smooth on 60, 120, 144, 240 and 360+ Hz displays.
.PP
Alien 14 (\fIAlbert Alienstein\fR) may carry a relativistic warp drive. Each
relativistic starship holds exactly two spacetime jumps. A player projectile
entering its proximity radius (2.4x the hull half-diagonal) is dodged before
impact: the jump is consumed, the physical colliders deactivate so the
projectile keeps its normal trajectory straight through the vacated space,
and the starship re-materializes in a free honeycomb cell at least five
Chebyshev cells away from both its previous station and the player ship. The
landing cell is drawn in constant time from the active formation minus both
exclusion zones, clamped inside the screen margins, cached for the whole
transit and then kept as the new permanent station. While at least one jump
remains no projectile can destroy it; only the tactical nuke kills a
starship in mid-warp.
.PP
With no arguments the game starts normally. The options below drive the
graphics driver, the audio engine, the headless soundtrack jukebox and its
exporter, the frame-hitch flight recorder, and the usual version/help
banners. Every flag is dash-agnostic:
one or more leading dashes are equivalent, so \fB\-play\fR, \fB\-\-play\fR and
\fB\-\-\-play\fR all select the same option.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-driver ", " \-d " \fIname\fR"
Launch the game with a specific 2D graphics driver
(\fBvulkan\fR, \fBopengl\fR, \fBopengles2\fR, \fBsoftware\fR).
.TP
.BR \-backends ", " \-b
List all 2D graphics rendering backends (SDL3 render drivers) supported on
the current display, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-list ", " \-l
Print the 15-movement classical soundtrack anthology (composer, work, movement,
scored length and one historical note per track), then exit.
.TP
.BR \-play ", " \-p " \fItracks\fR"
Play soundtrack movements in headless terminal mode with a live progress
bar. \fItracks\fR is a single number (\fB3\fR), an inclusive range
(\fB1 15\fR), or a comma-separated list in any order (\fB6,1,15,2,8\fR;
spaces around commas are accepted and a list may repeat tracks). Each
movement plays COMPLETE by default; \fB\-start\fR / \fB\-end\fR narrow
the window. Ctrl+C stops playback cleanly.
.TP
.B \-shuffle
Jukebox only: play the \fB\-play\fR selection (range or list) in random
order, drawing a fresh permutation per run (printed before
playback). Long form only: the short \fB\-s\fR belongs to \fB\-start\fR.
Requires \fB\-play\fR and cannot be combined with \fB\-output\fR,
which writes a single, fixed track.
.TP
.BR \-start ", " \-s " \fIsec\fR"
Jukebox only: open the playback window at \fIsec\fR seconds (default \fB0\fR).
Used together with \fB\-play\fR; accepted in any position on the command line,
with or without the short spelling \fB\-s\fR.
.TP
.BR \-end ", " \-e " \fIsec\fR"
Jukebox only: close the playback window at \fIsec\fR seconds. Omit it and the
movement plays to its end: the default window runs to the track's own
scored length, printed per track by \fB\-list\fR, and any value given
is clamped to it. Used together with \fB\-play\fR; accepted in any
position on the command line, with or without the short spelling
\fB\-e\fR.
.TP
.BR \-output ", " \-o " \fIfile\fR"
Jukebox only: write the selected window to \fIfile\fR instead of playing
it. WAV is written natively (zero dependencies); FLAC/MP3/OGG/Opus/M4A are
piped through an encoder found on PATH (\fBffmpeg\fR, \fBflac\fR,
\fBlame\fR, \fBoggenc\fR, \fBopusenc\fR), with a graceful WAV fallback when
none is installed. Combine with a single \fB\-play\fR track (no ranges) and
with the \fB\-start\fR/\fB\-end\fR window.
.TP
.BR \-render ", " \-r
Force the procedural synth renderer for the game and the jukebox. By
default the TinySoundFont engine renders through a GM-compatible SoundFont
bank (\fB.sf2\fR) whenever one is installed; with no bank found, the
procedural synth takes over automatically and a one-time terminal notice
recommends the MIT-licensed FluidR3 GM bank. Accepted in any position on
the command line, with or without the short spelling \fB\-r\fR.
.TP
.B \-log
Arm the frame-hitch flight recorder (same as \fBALIENS_HITCH_LOG=1\fR).
Each slow frame prints one aligned row naming the culprit phase
(input, simulation, render, present, pacing) and a verdict. The report
threshold defaults to 33.3 ms and is set with \fBALIENS_HITCH_MS\fR.
.TP
.BR \-version ", " \-v
Print the version banner (release, engine, license, repository) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-help ", " \-h
Display the command-line manual and option reference, then exit.
.SH SOUNDTRACK
Each movement is a public-domain classical work, synthesized at run time,
scored as a
.B one continuous performance at its own length
\- no internal seams. The anthology is scored as complete works, one
translation unit per movement (\fBsrc/musics/music_NN.cc\fR), and
\fB\-list\fR prints every track's exact scored length. The stage
fanfare heard in-game is the movement's climatic six seconds \- the window
[\fIpeak_start_seconds\fR, +6 s] published by the track's ScoreManifest,
frozen by ear per work (\fB0.0f\fR keeps the movement's opening) and
sealed by the shared 0.50 s fade-out. Both engines share one finishing
chain (hall reverb, an ear-guard high-shelf above ~4.2 kHz, the fades and
peak normalization to 0.92), and scores are regenerated from MIDI with the
repository tool \fBtools/midi2cpp\fR. The
jukebox plays any window inside the performance: by default the COMPLETE
movement (\fB0\fR to the track's own scored length); \fB\-start\fR/\fB\-s\fR
and \fB\-end\fR/\fB\-e\fR narrow it to any slice (as short as one second).
.PP
The anthology:
.PP
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 3
1.
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart - Rondo alla Turca (Turkish March), K. 331
.TP
2.
Carlos Gomes - O Guarani (Il Guarany Overture, complete: mm. 1-65)
.TP
3.
Giacomo Puccini - Turandot: Nessun Dorma
.TP
4.
Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky - Swan Lake (Danse des petits cygnes)
.TP
5.
Ludwig van Beethoven - Symphony No. 5 (The Fate Motif)
.TP
6.
Johann Sebastian Bach - Toccata and Fugue in D minor, BWV 565
.TP
7.
Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky - The Nutcracker: Waltz of the Flowers
.TP
8.
Maurice Ravel - Bolero
.TP
9.
Gioachino Rossini - The Barber of Seville: Overture
.TP
10.
Edvard Grieg - Peer Gynt: Morning Mood
.TP
11.
Zequinha de Abreu - Tico-Tico no Fuba
.TP
12.
Richard Wagner - Die Walkure: Ride of the Valkyries
.TP
13.
Frederic Chopin - Fantaisie-Impromptu, Op. 66
.TP
14.
Claude Debussy - Suite Bergamasque: Clair de Lune
.TP
15.
Antonio Vivaldi - The Four Seasons: Spring
.PD
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ALIENS_HITCH_LOG
Set to \fB1\fR to arm the frame-hitch flight recorder (same as \fB\-log\fR).
.TP
.B ALIENS_HITCH_MS
Report threshold in milliseconds for the flight recorder (default 33.3;
accepted range 4..2000).
.TP
.B ALIENS_INVADERS_PLAYER
Callsign identifying you in the multi-user Hall of Fame. Fallback order
when unset: \fBALIENS_INVADERS_PSEUDO\fR (legacy alias), the Steam persona
name (\fBSteamPersonName\fR), then the login user
(\fBUSER\fR/\fBLOGNAME\fR/\fBUSERNAME\fR).
.TP
.B ALIENS_SOUNDFONT
Path to a GM-compatible SoundFont bank (\fB.sf2\fR) for the TinySoundFont
engine; an absolute path is recommended, since the working directory may
vary. Checked before the directory search (see FILES).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (game closed normally, or the requested banner/jukebox run finished).
.TP
.B 1
A command-line option was unknown or badly formed, or a requested subsystem
(audio device, graphics driver) failed to start.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
aliens-invaders                       # launch the game
aliens-invaders -driver opengl        # launch with OpenGL
aliens-invaders -list                 # print the anthology
aliens-invaders -play 3               # track 3, complete (the default)
aliens-invaders -play 3 -s 6 -e 30    # track 3, a slice from second 6 to 30
aliens-invaders -play 3 -s 41 -e 47   # audition a climatic preset window
aliens-invaders -play 1 15            # the whole anthology, each track in full
aliens-invaders -play 6,1,15,2,8      # exactly these tracks, in this order
aliens-invaders -play 1 15 -shuffle   # the anthology in random order
aliens-invaders -play 5 -e 30 -output m5.flac  # write track 5, 0-30 s, FLAC
aliens-invaders -render               # procedural synth instead of the bank
aliens-invaders -log                  # launch with the hitch recorder armed
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I aliens-invaders.scores
Arcade high-score tables (multi-user Hall of Fame). Written to the shared
\fB/var/games/aliens-invaders.scores\fR on Linux/FreeBSD when that file
exists and is writable; otherwise to the user save directory
(\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/aliens-invaders\fR, defaulting to
\fB~/.local/share/aliens-invaders\fR on Linux; the roaming \fBAPPDATA\fR
folder on Windows; the platform preference path on macOS and mobile). A
legacy \fB./aliens-invaders.scores\fR in the working directory is migrated
into the user save directory on first run. Every row ends with a salted,
truncated SHA-256 digest column computed over the row's exact contents: a
hand-edited or forged row fails verification and is silently dropped at
load, so the leaderboard only trusts runs the game itself signed.
.TP
.I *.sf2
Optional GM-compatible SoundFont bank for the TinySoundFont engine
(FluidR3 GM recommended; ties break alphabetically within a directory).
Search order: \fB$ALIENS_SOUNDFONT\fR,
\fB./assets/soundfonts\fR,
\fB~/.local/share/aliens-invaders/soundfonts\fR,
\fB~/.local/share/soundfonts\fR,
\fB/usr/local/share/aliens-invaders/soundfonts\fR,
\fB/usr/local/share/soundfonts\fR,
\fB/usr/share/aliens-invaders/soundfonts\fR, \fB/usr/share/soundfonts\fR;
macOS adds \fB/Library/Audio/Sounds/Banks\fR. The first directory holding
a bank wins.
.SH AUTHOR
Claudio Fernandes de Souza Rodrigues.
